    "body": "### Problem\n\nA window inside a vertical split can be \"pushed\" into the status line by a window above it that has a winbar, causing its first row to overlap with the status line. This happens when:\n\n1. The global status line is enabled (`set laststatus=3`)\n2. The adjacent windows are in a vertical split\n3. The bottom window has a single row height\n4. The top window has a winbar\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82762daf-014c-46bb-b461-84431a1d9f6a\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\ncat << EOF > winbar_bug.lua\nvim.opt.laststatus = 3\n\n-- only repros on vsplit windows\nvim.cmd(\"vsplit\")\n\nvim.cmd(\"split\")\n\n-- bottom-left window\nvim.api.nvim_win_set_height(0, 1)\n\n-- top-left window\nvim.wo.winbar = 'hello'\nvim.api.nvim_win_set_height(0, 1000)\nEOF\n\nnvim --clean -u winbar_bug.lua\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe bottom-left window does not overlap the status line.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1209+g794886aae7\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, vim 9.2.907\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nFrom source, no modifications, `make nvim`",
